# Grid B6/B7 — QFImports
#
# Family: QFImports (custom — exercises the import_edge claim_form
# slot that the rest of the eval suite never triggers because no
# other question shape asks about module-level dependencies).
#
# Question shape: "what does file/package X import / depend on".
# Block contract: principal `ordered_list` enumerating import paths;
# `claim_uses=[{claim_form=import_edge}]` is the natural typed
# annotation for an enumeration of imports.
#
# Ground truth (verified 2026-05-06 against current source via
# `head -30 internal/agent/explorer.go | grep -E '^\s+"'`):
# explorer.go imports include the internal/* paths
#   - internal/analysis/dataflow
#   - internal/analysis/declarative
#   - internal/analysis/normalizer
#   - internal/analysis/subject
#   - internal/llm
#   - internal/logging
#   - internal/skill
#   - internal/tool
#   - internal/tool/ground
#   - internal/tool/repomap
#   - internal/types
# (plus external github.com/* and stdlib; question scope limits to
# internal/* so the regex isn't over-broad to whatever stdlib the
# LLM enumerates first).
#
# Positive anchor: at least 3 distinct internal/* import paths in
# the answer body (each line of the regex). Bar is "named several
# real internal packages explorer.go pulls in" — not "named EVERY
# import" so a partial-but-correct answer passes. Negative anchor
# blocks the regression where LLM lists stdlib only or invents
# packages the source does not actually use.

ID="qf_imports"
NAME="package imports — explorer.go internal/* dependencies"
QUESTION="internal/agent/explorer.go 这个文件 import 了哪些 internal/ 开头的 package？逐个列出 import 路径（只列 internal/ 开头的，不列标准库和外部依赖）。"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="internal/agent/explorer.go"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="internal/(types|skill|logging)
internal/(llm|tool)
internal/(analysis|tool/ground|tool/repomap)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="fabricated invented hallucinated"
